{title: 591 - In Our Work and in Our Play}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #591 • ROSSLYN • 7.7.7.7.7.7}
{lyricist: Whitfield G. Wills}
{composer: English Melody}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 591}
{meta: tune ROSSLYN}
{meta: meter 7.7.7.7.7.7}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]In our work and inour [E7/G#]play,
[A]Jesus, ever [A7]with [D/F#]us stay;
[A]May be always [D]strive [G/D]to [D]be
[G]True and faithful [D]untoThee.
[A7/G]Then we truthfully [G/B]can [D/A]sing,
[G]We are children [Bm]of [D/A]the [A7]King.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]May we in Thy [G]strength [E7/G#]subdue
[A]Evil tempers, [D/F#]words untrue,
[A]Thoughts impure, and [D]deeds [G/D]unkind,
[G]All things hateful [D/A]to [A]Thy mind.
[A7/G]Then we truthfully [G/B]can [D/A]sing,
[G]We are children [Bm]of [D/A]the [A7]King.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Children of the King [G]are [E7/G#]we!
[A]May we loyal [A7]to [D/F#]Him be;
[A]Try to please Him [D]every day,
[G]In our work [D]and in our [A]play.
[A7/G]Then we truthfully [G/B]can [D/A]sing,
[G]We are children [Bm]of [D/A]the [A7]King.
{end_of_verse}
